WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:01.400 --> 00:06.220
A difficult conversation can be a great way
to build your interpersonal skills.

2
00:06.280 --> 00:08.060
Yes, hear me out.

3
00:08.120 --> 00:12.140
What if you didn't allow potentially difficult conversations to drain you,

4
00:12.200 --> 00:16.780
and instead, used them as a means
to cultivate strong relationships?

5
00:17.320 --> 00:22.220
In the face of a difficult conversation,
you may feel as if you're standing at a doorstep.

6
00:22.280 --> 00:27.900
It may be that you're looking at a closed door in front of you,
fearing what you may encounter on the other side.

7
00:27.960 --> 00:33.180
So you're just standing there paralyzed,
and unwilling to open the mysterious door.

8
00:33.240 --> 00:37.100
Or it may be that you are ready to open the door,
but you are dreading it.

9
00:37.160 --> 00:42.700
Your mindset is fixed, and you believe
that nothing good can come out of the conversation.

10
00:42.840 --> 00:46.254
In either case, you may make up stories about the other person.

11
00:46.314 --> 00:52.494
Perhaps you don't appreciate some of their characteristics,
and you blame them for making you feel uneasy.

12
00:52.554 --> 00:55.054
Or you may make up stories about yourself.

13
00:55.114 --> 01:02.174
For example, thinking this will ruin your already shaky relationship,
or that you'll end up with a bad reputation.

14
01:02.394 --> 01:09.454
You may start feeling guilt or shame,
or experience physical symptoms, like a racing heart or nausea.

15
01:09.594 --> 01:15.534
Other times you may rationalize it:
“It isn't a good time, I'm too busy for this.”

16
01:15.594 --> 01:21.134
All the while, the door to a more resilient
and productive relationship remains shut.

17
01:21.194 --> 01:23.774
Here's a tip. Be curious.

18
01:23.834 --> 01:30.588
Open the door with a resilient mindset and with attention,
vulnerability, empathy, and compassion.

19
01:30.808 --> 01:38.908
Because even a potentially difficult conversation is actually an opportunity
to build a stronger, more meaningful relationship.

20
01:39.368 --> 01:48.988
Some very common examples of difficult conversations are
tough performance dialogues, feedback conversations, and team discussions.

21
01:49.368 --> 01:53.808
It can be tempting to leave the doors to those conversations closed.
